    RESULT: PASS — the pads sweep from clear of the cube to closed past it, so a
    flat parallel grip is geometrically possible.

    WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW
    A free-space sweep says nothing about whether a grasp HOLDS. The known failure
    mode is the cube wedging on the curved proximal r1/l1 links: that survives a
    static hold test and fails under lift accelerations. The next script has to
    close on the cube and check the pads stall at the cube width, not wider.

    TCP OFFSET: read tcp_from_wrist at q=0.00 above as the STARTING value for the
    env's ee_frame OffsetCfg. It is a starting value, not the answer — the pad
    midpoint travels 0.0282 m over the stroke, so the
    TCP is not a fixed point. Calibrate it against a real grasp before trusting it.

